agree, do not download, install or use the Software.

0.3. Rights that are not expressly granted in this License are not granted (Civil Code of the Russian
Federation, Article 1235(1)).

### 1. Definitions

- **Software**: the Zorcam NVR program (community edition) published by the Licensor: the source code, the
  official distributions (archives, .deb packages) and the documentation, in every version. It includes any
  part of these and any Modification of them.
- **Official Sources**: the repository `https://github.com/davydovv-creator/zorcam-nvr-community` and other
  places the Licensor names in that repository.
- **Your Devices**: computers (for example, a Raspberry Pi) that you own or lawfully control for your own needs.
- **Modification**: any change to the Software, translation or adaptation of it, or a work based on it.
- **Third-Party Components**: programs that are not part of the Software and that the Software uses or that its
  installer downloads, under their own licenses (Section 6).
- **Zorcam Cloud**: the online service of the Licensor (or of a person named by him) for remote access to
  Zorcam devices, offered under separate terms.

### 2. What you may do

Subject to the conditions of this License, the Licensor grants you, free of charge, for the whole term of the
copyright in the Software and in all countries of the world, a non-exclusive, non-transferable license, without
the right to grant sublicenses, to:

2.1. download the Software from the Official Sources and reproduce it as far as needed to install, run, update
and back it up on Your Devices;

2.2. read and study the source code;

2.3. install and use the Software on any number of Your Devices for the purposes of Section 3;

2.4. make Modifications for your own use on Your Devices, subject to Section 4;

2.5. fork the repository on GitHub using GitHub's own functionality, solely to view the code and to prepare and
submit contributions (issues, pull requests) under `CONTRIBUTING.md` and the Zorcam Contributor License
Agreement.

### 3. Permitted purposes

3.1. You may use the Software for personal, family and household purposes.

3.2. You may also use it in your own business or professional activity, for example to watch your own shop,
office, warehouse or site. A person (for example, an installer) may install the Software on Your Devices on your
behalf. That person may charge for their work but not for the Software itself.

3.3. You may let your family members, employees and guests view your cameras through the Software.

3.4. Without a separate written agreement with the Licensor, you may not use the Software to provide services to
third parties. This includes hosted or "as a service" video surveillance, remote monitoring for other people, and
operating the Software on devices you provide to customers.

### 4. What you may not do

Unless the Licensor agrees in writing, you may not:

4.1. sell, rent, lease, lend for a fee or otherwise commercially provide the Software or copies of it, or grant
sublicenses;

4.2. sell, rent or lease devices with the Software (or a Modification) pre-installed, or bundle the Software with
any product or service you sell, except as allowed in Section 5;

4.3. publish or distribute the Software, Modifications, forks or builds of them (in source or binary form, as
